WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.940
Four Years Earlier

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.160
Excuse me.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:14.020
May I take a seat next to you?

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:16.120
Of course. Go right ahead.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.040
Thank you.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:21.410
You will be receiving a call.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:22.500
Here.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:25.270
Take it.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.430
Please pick up the call.

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:37.090
Hello and nice to meet you.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.390
Who are you?

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:43.070
I am... Well, I'm a witch.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:44.890
Please tell me your name.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:49.020
I'm sorry. I don't have one.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.070
What are you calling me for?

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.280
How old are you?

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.830
I'm a sixth year in elementary school.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.330
I see. Are you alone?

00:00:58.330 --> 00:00:59.400
Yes, ma'am.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.940
That's impressive!

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.160
Where are you headed?

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.750
I'm going over to visit my grandpa's house.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:08.730
My parents will be coming
a little late because of work.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:10.500
That's a lie, isn't it?

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.740
What makes you think that?

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:15.010
I don't need to have a reason.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.510
You already know the answer to that.

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:21.160
What in the world do you know about me?

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:24.020
I know almost nothing about you.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:31.360
But if I had to say, I do know that you're somehow
dissatisfied about the current state of this world.

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:34.280
How do you know that?

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:37.020
That's because I'm a witch.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:40.410
I don't believe in witches.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:43.340
And I'm not dissatisfied about anything.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:46.800
Why did you board the train, then?

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:51.570
It's because you're looking
for a place where you belong.

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:54.300
I don't believe such a place exists.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:59.390
It does! The place where you belong
is what lies ahead on that train route.

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:03.310
But if you set foot there, you will never
be able to return to your normal life.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.840
Because that is where you belong.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:08.170
It will grab on to you and never let go.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:11.660
Take a look out the window.

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:15.370
You mustn't go past those mountains.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:19.490
Do not set foot in the town that lies beyond them.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.580
That's Sakurada, isn't it?

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:23.900
Correct.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:27.000
Sakurada will grab on to you and never let go.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:34.960
Asai Kei, if you love the world you currently
live in, then get off at the next station.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:38.190
How do you know my name?

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:39.870
How do you think I know?

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.510
Because you're a witch.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:46.290
Congratulations. You're correct!

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:22.610
A certain woman wants to see you and Haruki.

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:25.360
First Time
Wednesday
August 9th

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.430
Who is this "certain woman"?

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:29.800
She's near the top of the ladder in the Bureau.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:32.360
We're not allowed to turn down her summons.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:37.240
Dammit. I didn't want to get
you two involved with her.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:38.400
Why is that?

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.610
I'm not allowed to talk about her.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:45.340
But let's just say she's the most dangerous
person to deal with in Sakurada.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.840
Tomorrow morning, a member of
the Bureau will come to pick you up.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.050
Go without putting up a fight. Got it?

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:55.850
Are you Asai?

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:57.960
Yes.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:00.690
You're Mr. Sasano, right?

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:02.540
Perfect timing.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:05.200
I just went to a Japanese sweets shop nearby.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.200
Their azuki bean jelly is delicious.

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:18.920
Why do you want the MacGuffin?

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:22.240
I want to get my ability back.

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:28.320
If the MacGuffin controls the abilities in Sakurada,
then it might be possible to do so.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:30.100
Did you lose your ability?

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.460
Yeah.

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:37.180
Last week, I was visited by a girl
who said she'd seal my ability away.

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:40.230
I haven't been able to use my ability ever since.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:44.050
What kind of ability do you possess, Mr. Sasano?

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:46.240
I'll show you.

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:58.720
These are pictures I took of my yard.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:00.710
That's a very beautiful cherry blossom tree.

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:03.380
It's from twenty years ago.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:07.720
All the pictures in this album
are ones I took while using my ability.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:09.840
While using your ability?

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:15.050
The things I've lost are in these pictures.

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:19.100
But with my ability, I'm able to restore things.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.880
What do you mean?

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:23.880
My ability recreates the past.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:27.330
You can think of it as an ability
to enter a photograph.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:29.180
Just for a little bit, though.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:31.870
So, you're saying you're able to enter photographs?

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:37.410
If I use my ability and tear up
a photo, I can go into it.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:40.720
I wish I could show you how
it actually works, though.

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:41.750
That's too bad.

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:44.350
There are a lot of restrictions, too.

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:48.720
When I tear up the photo, I have to be in
the same spot where the picture was taken.

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:51.440
I have about ten minutes inside it,

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:54.180
and when time's up,
I'm forced back into the real world.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:07:02.500
I gaze upon the nostalgic scenery,
take in familiar scents, and speak with old faces.

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:06.230
It's just an ability to immerse
yourself in your memories.

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:09.660
I see. I think I understand now.

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:14.030
Will you lend me the MacGuffin?

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:20.040
Well, I don't think the MacGuffin
has any special powers.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:20.710
Huh?

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:26.840
I think you lost your ability due to
the ability of the girl who visited you.

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:32.270
And if that is the case, then finding a way to cancel
out her ability is the surefire way of getting it back.

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:34.600
I don't have the slightest idea how to do that.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:37.280
I can help you out with that.

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:39.720
I'm a member of the Service Club.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:41.100
"Service Club"?

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:45.320
I'm sort of like a volunteer who deals
with matters concerning special abilities.

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:48.360
Please tell me about the girl who visited you.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:51.550
She looked about your age.

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:56.200
She wore distressed jeans, a cross choker,

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.620
and her eyes were red.

00:07:57.900 --> 00:07:59.210
Her eyes were red?

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:01.500
She said they were colored contacts.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:04.380
When did this red-eyed girl come by?

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:08.500
I think it was around 5 in
the evening on August 3rd.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:10.280
<i>Six days ago, huh?</i>

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:12.110
<i>We can't go back to that day with a reset.</i>

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:25.400
Oh, the sunset was so beautiful
that I took that one on a whim.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:28.610
The contrast between the sunlight
and shadows is splendid, isn't it?

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:31.610
<i>Is that the MacGuffin?</i>

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:37.130
How did you find out that I have the MacGuffin?

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:39.640
I heard from a friend in the Bureau.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:41.690
May I ask who that might be?

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:44.560
Sorry, I can't answer that.

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:45.710
I see.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:50.340
Also, how should I repay you?

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:53.800
We don't accept any compensation
for Service Club activities.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:56.720
But I'll feel bad if I don't.

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:58.480
Is that so?

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:05.290
Then, if everything goes well,
would you use your ability for me?

00:09:06.890 --> 00:09:08.630
Hello, Murase?

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:09.730
What do you want?

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:12.430
I've got two things I'd like to ask of you.

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:14.480
First, I want you to find someone for me.

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:15.730
And the second thing?

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:18.910
There's someone who got his ability
sealed by someone else's ability.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:21.120
I want you to erase the effect of the sealing ability.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:23.340
There are three problems with that.

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:27.830
The first problem is that I can
only erase things for 5 minutes.

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:31.590
Secondly, I've never erased an ability
that was placed on a person before.

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:34.840
And lastly, I've gotten weaker.

00:09:35.110 --> 00:09:36.450
What do you mean?

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:40.760
Ever since that day, I've been unable
to use my ability to target people.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:46.030
I see. Sorry.

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:48.800
I think it was for the best.

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:52.540
I'm sure there was a better way to go about it.

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:54.380
It's just that I wasn't capable of it.

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:55.440
I'm surprised.

00:09:56.020 --> 00:09:59.630
I thought you were always
brimming with confidence.

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:01.760
I'm not like that.

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:03.700
Shall I cheer you up?

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:06.870
What you did was right.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:09.480
That's very charming of you to say.

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:13.640
Liar. I'm sure that isn't what you wanted.

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:17.030
No way. I love it when people are kind to me.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:22.760
Well, whatever. I'm still grateful for what you did.

00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:25.940
It was all part of Mr. Tsushima's plan.

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:28.480
That's why I'll seriously show
up to my remedial classes.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:31.560
About what we talked about before...

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:33.360
Did you find out anything?

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:34.840
I'm not sure.

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:37.150
Everything about it seems completely false.

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:41.030
It's enough to make me doubt
the existence of the MacGuffin.

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:43.660
The story is too far-fetched.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:48.690
Can a person who possesses the MacGuffin really
have control over all of the abilities in Sakurada?

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:52.610
So basically, you're saying the MacGuffin
is just a baseless rumor, huh?

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:55.800
At this point, it would be right
to arrive at that conclusion.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.780
But I have the MacGuffin.

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:00.730
That's the problem.

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:05.260
This type of rumor typically doesn't take hold.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:08.260
The rumor popped up just two years ago.

00:11:08.260 --> 00:11:13.230
It sure is unusual for such an unbelievable
rumor to spread so suddenly.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:17.990
If the rumor was randomly spread
by someone, then they're incredibly brilliant.

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:20.290
I've got another favor.

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:24.640
Could you look into a person
named Sasano Hiroyuki?

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:26.780
Why do you want to know about that person?

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:29.710
He wants the MacGuffin.

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:32.180
"Sasano Hiroyuki"...

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:34.960
He's a pretty fascinating person!

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:40.220
He retired three years ago after being
assigned to city hall 28 years ago.

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:42.220
The problem is what came before that.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:45.550
Before that, he had worked
for the Bureau for ten years.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:47.600
Does that have any real significance?

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:51.000
It does. It has an extremely major significance.

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:54.590
It means he was with the Bureau 38 years ago.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:58.040
That's the year when special abilities
were first observed in Sakurada

00:11:58.040 --> 00:12:00.240
and when the Bureau was established.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:04.910
Sasano Hiroyuki is a founding
member of the Bureau.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:08.370
First Time
Thursday
August 10th

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:12.060
Good morning, Kei.

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:13.800
Morning, Haruki.

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:15.630
Did you eat breakfast?

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:18.390
Not yet. I just woke up.

00:12:18.390 --> 00:12:20.130
How about we eat together?

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:22.490
I made some sandwiches.

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:24.240
Thanks for doing that.

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:26.700
By the way, can I ask you a favor?

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:27.850
What is it?

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:31.110
I still need to get changed,
so I'd like you to give me three minutes.

00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:33.120
I don't mind.

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:34.810
I sort of do, though.

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:37.390
All right, then.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:51.200
What are you thinking about?

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:53.330
About the Swampman.

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:55.680
What is the Swampman?

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:57.570
It's a kind of thought experiment.

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:02.840
A man happens to pass by a swamp and
ends up getting struck and killed by lightning.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:06.000
But you assume that another lightning bolt
strikes the swamp at the same time,

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:08.410
and a new identical life is created from the swamp

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:13.310
with the same appearance, knowledge,
and personality as the dead man.

00:13:13.780 --> 00:13:18.320
The Swampman believes he is the dead man,

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:21.050
but he doesn't know that he was hit by lightning.

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:24.780
In this situation, what does the Swampman do?

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:28.910
Doesn't he act as if he is the dead man?

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:30.160
Yeah.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:33.190
And no one notices that the man died.

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:36.740
Do you think that the man
died even in this situation?

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:39.880
Yes. In reality, he is dead.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:45.320
Then, what's the difference between
the dead man and the Swampman?

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:47.760
That's the subject of this thought experiment.

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:56.020
Kei, how would you feel if I died and someone
who looks exactly like me appeared?

00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:01.330
I'd feel sad... really sad.

00:14:01.330 --> 00:14:05.930
Do you think you'd be better off not knowing?

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:09.240
No, I don't think I would.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:11.030
Thank you very much.

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:12.030
For what?

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:13.880
Just because.

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:17.660
I think I'm just happy to hear that from you.

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:19.420
That's good, then.

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.690
Yes, it is.

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:29.610
I'm from the Bureau.

00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:31.200
I've come to pick you up.

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.580
Haruki, please enter this room.

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:55.340
Just Haruki?

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:58.410
Yes, you'll be sent in one at a time.

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:00.940
Catch you later.

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:02.670
Okay. I'll see you later.

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:14.050
This way, please.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:31.940
It's been a long time.

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:36.080
Or should I say, nice to meet you?

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:39.960
May I ask what your name is?

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:43.620
I'm sorry. I don't have one.

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:46.710
I'm not sure how I should address you, then.

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:51.280
I'm an entity that essentially needs no name.

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:53.990
Call me "Witch," if you must.

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:03.270
He locks the door with his right hand
and unlocks it with his left.

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:07.150
A door that he closes with
his ability will never open.

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:10.090
You're protected by two doors, then.

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:12.920
No, I'm being confined in here.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:16.200
There's nothing connecting
me to the outside world.

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:16.990
What about that?

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:22.460
It's only connected to one place,
and the person I speak to is always the same.

00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:26.470
How did you call me four years ago?

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:28.940
I had to go through a lot of trouble.

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:31.170
And I prepared some
justifications for my actions, too.

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:34.430
Come a bit closer.

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:40.100
Bend down a little.

00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:48.900
I wanted to see you, Asai Kei.

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:52.320
I've always wanted to apologize to you.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:54.070
For what?

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:57.620
For making you come to Sakurada.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:16:59.920
You gave me a warning.

00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:02.600
I came to this town of my own free will.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:04.340
No.

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:09.960
I knew that if I called you,
you would definitely come to this town.

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:13.470
What kind of entity are you?

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:17.900
Think of me as a system—a tool, basically.

00:17:17.900 --> 00:17:23.180
I am a part of the system that was necessary
to create, develop, and maintain the Bureau.

00:17:23.530 --> 00:17:26.100
Did you create the Bureau?

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:28.020
Not quite.

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:32.310
The ones who created the Bureau
are the people who used my ability.

00:17:32.310 --> 00:17:36.440
I can learn of someone's future.

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:38.200
You can learn the future?

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:41.390
That's the ability I possess.

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:45.160
I am the system that observes
the future of Sakurada.

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:50.520
It's been close to 30 years
since I've been isolated like this.

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:54.300
Could you go into detail about your ability?

00:17:55.770 --> 00:17:58.640
First, I touch someone, then close my eyes.

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:03.000
And then a door being opened comes to my mind.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.600
If I do that, I can see the person's future.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:11.610
I can experience what that person
will see and hear someday.

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:14.820
Did you see my future just now?

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:18.060
It was very refreshing.

00:18:18.060 --> 00:18:22.030
I always see my own future, after all.

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:26.840
If a problem arises in Sakurada,
the information will come to me.

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:31.940
If I see my own future, I'll know the exact problem.

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:37.170
And if I see a future where I receive that
information, I report it over the phone.

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:41.350
Does that mean you change the future?

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:46.260
Due to my correspondence, the future changes,
and the problem is avoided before it happens.

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:49.560
That's why no one really visits this room.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:51.980
Would you tell me about my future?

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:53.890
I can't do that.

00:18:53.890 --> 00:18:58.590
I'm not authorized to tell the future for individuals.

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:05.660
Meeting with you today was
an extremely special case, you know.

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:10.140
I can say it was a system error—
a problem that needed to be corrected.

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:11.750
A problem?

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:18.120
Yes. But I needed to see your future no matter what.

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:19.040
Why?

00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:21.260
I can't answer that.

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:24.920
If I tell you the reason,
I'll end up telling you the future.

00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:29.700
It's also the reason we have you and
Haruki Misora visiting my room separately.

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:31.650
It was to prevent a reset, wasn't it?

00:19:31.950 --> 00:19:35.560
Still, there's one thing about
the future that I can tell you.

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:38.150
I'm going to die soon.

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:45.000
I've known of my final days since long ago.

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:47.910
It's a future I've gotten used to.

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:58.920
By the way, why are you a witch?

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:02.030
It was something I heard a long time ago.

00:20:02.030 --> 00:20:04.180
A story of a witch who rode on a broom,

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:08.270
flying through the sky to knock on
the window of her beloved's room.

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:10.930
I've been longing to do that.

00:20:14.490 --> 00:20:16.170
Looks like time's up.

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:18.370
Thank you very much.

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:19.880
Pardon me.

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:23.700
I'm sorry.

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:27.410
I don't regret coming to Sakurada.

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:32.660
No, not that. I'm apologizing for something else.

00:20:33.610 --> 00:20:34.710
Farewell.

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:37.970
<i>A witch who can predict the future...</i>

00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:40.460
Hey there!

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:54.900
What makes you fall in love with someone?

00:20:56.850 --> 00:21:00.360
I suppose something like their thought process...

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:06.160
Specifically, what they think under each
circumstance and what kind of action they will take.

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:08.900
Do you understand his thoughts?

00:21:08.900 --> 00:21:09.910
I don't.

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:12.000
Can you fall in love with
someone you don't understand?

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:15.300
Even without fully understanding,
there's things I can be sure of.

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:18.350
Can you fall in love with a stone?

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:21.590
I don't particularly like stones.

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:26.320
In that case, let's imagine that his body
has transformed into a pebble.

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:31.960
It's a cold pebble that doesn't
speak or move. All it can do is think.

00:21:32.580 --> 00:21:35.610
Can you fall in love with that stone?

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:36.980
Yes, I can.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:43.250
Then, what's the difference between a thinking stone
and an ordinary stone lying by the road?

00:21:43.250 --> 00:21:46.250
What do you expect from a stone that thinks?

00:21:46.250 --> 00:21:47.740
Nothing.

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:49.180
Really?

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:50.120
Yes.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:55.280
I see. Your problem is your tendency
to agree to everything so easily.

00:21:55.280 --> 00:21:56.870
What do you mean?

00:21:57.120 --> 00:22:01.450
If you're telling the truth, then you should live
on and hold that pebble close to you forever.

00:22:01.450 --> 00:22:05.590
You can believe that his will
is in it and die knowing that.

00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:11.780
No, if he desires it from the bottom of his heart,
his voice will reach me someday.

00:22:11.780 --> 00:22:15.350
And that stone will return
to being a human, if necessary.

00:22:15.350 --> 00:22:16.520
Is that so?

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:20.180
If that's the case, why do you not desire anything?

00:22:20.180 --> 00:22:25.250
After all, you should wish for the stone
to speak and return to being human.

00:22:25.250 --> 00:22:27.260
It's because there's no need to.

00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:30.130
So the only thing that's important is his thoughts?

00:22:30.130 --> 00:22:31.030
Yes.

00:22:31.030 --> 00:22:35.750
Now, let's take his thoughts out of the stone.

00:22:35.750 --> 00:22:41.790
Can you throw it away when it actually
turns into an ordinary stone?

00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:46.060
What do you love about him?

00:22:46.550 --> 00:22:48.180
I don't know.

00:22:48.180 --> 00:22:50.300
What is the purpose of this discussion?

00:22:50.300 --> 00:22:52.240
There is none.

00:22:52.240 --> 00:22:55.350
I just wanted to chat with a girl about love.

00:22:56.310 --> 00:22:57.810
It's about time.

00:22:58.040 --> 00:23:00.960
I'm sorry to have you come all the way out here.

00:23:00.960 --> 00:23:01.900
Not at all.

00:23:01.900 --> 00:23:04.360
You better hurry.

00:23:04.360 --> 00:23:07.740
Asai Kei is talking to a girl right now.

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:12.950
Long time no see, Oka.

00:23:12.950 --> 00:23:15.060
Eww. What the hell?

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:17.840
Drop the formalities and call me
by my full name just like old times.

00:23:17.840 --> 00:23:19.080
"Oka Eri."

00:23:19.080 --> 00:23:22.210
Well then, Oka Eri, why are you here?

00:23:22.350 --> 00:23:22.510
We're always simply standing in a rain of eternal sadness

00:23:22.510 --> 00:23:24.220
It was just by chance!

00:23:24.220 --> 00:23:27.630
I was super surprised,
'cause my serious-looking upperclassman is here.

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:29.470
So I thought I'd have some fun by teasing you.

00:23:29.470 --> 00:23:30.970
That is why I need that warmth of yours

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:34.150
You surprised me. You've changed quite a bit.
